{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792421021,"nonce":"DJuwKAArST/W/hOwE/ybxHR/TxE=","title":"blinc_gpu: draw ABI backdrop records in paint order","message":"Display-list kind 42 is currently reported as Unsupported::Kind. It carries a Gaussian deviation in target pixels, a colour matrix, grain and opacity, and optionally liquid-glass bevel, rim, tint, border and dispersion. The geometry can be transformed or notched and takes screen/local/fade/element-frame clips.\n\nImplement an ordered backdrop item in display_list::plan. Read only pixels already painted at that point, including previous backdrops, and keep layer backdrop roots isolated. Use the ABI's Gaussian and premultiplied sampling, then its straight-colour matrix, coverage and glass formulas. Preserve the native glass pipeline and the ABI schema. Reuse shared Gaussian weights and distance/clip helpers; keep new modules below 1,000 lines. Avoid requiring extra usages on the caller's target texture.\n\nVerify real fixtures from the blinc_abi encoder, GPU-free decode and shader validation, and offscreen pixel comparisons against an independent CPU oracle at display scales 1 and 2. Cover paint order, transparent sources, transformed/clipped/notched backdrops, liquid rims and dispersion, overlapping backdrops and nested layers. Break snapshot order or frame translation to confirm tests reject it, restore the code, then run the full workspace gate. Record adapter and unverified platforms. Existing DSL baseline failures remain under a33d2b9; stale SDF data-texture packing remains under ce34b20.\n\nPart of fa2406c22865113e3900a06f340b9d4c0350f7266bd3afe01136c136e9f3409c.","files":null}]}